# Agile Logbook

**Project:** Tech Empower | **Subject:** Project Presentation 3 (PRP370S/371S/372S)

## Evidence

- 🗂️ [Tech Empower Trello board](https://trello.com/b/NqVLW18P/tech-empower3)

## What the logbook is

A record of the team's day-to-day work: stand-ups, sprint plans and retrospective
notes. Our charter set the ceremonies this logbook follows.

| Ceremony | How often | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Daily stand-up | Daily (15 min) | Sync on the Trello board and deal with blockers |
| Planning | Every 2 weeks | Prioritise new targets or modules |
| Review / demo | End of sprint | Show completed work |
| Retrospective | End of sprint | Discuss how to improve collaboration |

## Team activity from Trello

These entries come from the board's activity history (the latest 1,000
recorded actions).

| Date | What the team did on the board |
|---|---|
| 14 - 15 Jul 2026 | Sprint 1, Day 1 "Form the Project Team" scheduled on the board |
| 23 Jul 2026 | First recorded work on the board: members added to cards, checklist items ticked on several cards and cards such as the Sprint 1 and Sprint 2 stories marked complete (Pule, Tumelo and Jabu) |
| 24 Jul 2026 | Tumelo ticked checklist items on 11 cards and marked "Sprint 3. Create Google Forms Survey", "Sprint 3. Share Survey with Learners" and "Sprint 5. Write Business Description" complete; Jabu marked "Plan Customer Survey" complete |
| 6 Aug 2026 | Jabu ticked checklist items on 11 cards and marked daily cards complete, including Select Business Idea, Create Trello Board, Identify Target Community, Create Google Forms Survey and Share Survey with Learners |
| 21 Oct 2026 | Tumelo marked "Sprint 6. Plan Computer Lab Installation Service" complete |
| 27 Oct 2026 | Jabu completed the three Sprint 9 daily cards and the Sprint 9 About Us, Services, Contact and Products page cards |

## How the board shows our ceremonies

| Ceremony | What the board shows |
|---|---|
| Daily stand-up | Members added to cards and checklist items ticked on the dates in the table above. No separate stand-up notes were written on the cards. |
| Planning | Sprint columns with daily cards, and Sprint 1 Day 1 scheduled for 14 - 15 Jul 2026. |
| Review / demo | The Sprint 9 cards for the About Us, Services, Contact and Products pages were completed on 27 Oct 2026. |
| Retrospective | The backlog card "Conduct Sprint Retrospective" had not been completed, so no retrospective was recorded on the board. |

## Retrospective (written from the board evidence)

**What went well**
- Sprints 1 and 2 were completed in full, with every daily card's five tasks
  ticked.
- The team kept one structure throughout: a card per day with a five-task
  checklist.
- All the Sprint 9 website cards were completed.

**What did not go well**
- Board updates came in bursts (23 - 24 Jul, 6 Aug, 27 Oct) instead of daily as
  our charter says.
- Sprints 4 to 8 were never given their own columns, and the last Sprint 3 card
  is not marked complete.
- No stand-up or retrospective notes were recorded on the cards.

**What we should change**
- Update Trello the same day, as the charter says.
- Close each sprint properly and run the retrospective at its end.
- Add a short comment on a card for each stand-up, so the logbook has notes to
  show.

## Reflection

**What we did:** We used Trello as the record of our work and followed the
ceremonies in our team charter, from daily stand-ups to the sprint review and
retrospective.

**What I learned:**
- The activity history shows that our board updates came in bursts (23 and 24
  Jul, 6 Aug and 27 Oct) instead of daily. Our charter says to update Trello in
  real time, so the board did not always match the work.
- A logbook with dates shows how long the work really took, which a plain task
  list cannot.
- The closing cards in the backlog (Conduct Sprint Retrospective, Document
  Lessons Learned) had not been completed, so the retrospective needs to be
  written up properly.
- Without notes written at the time, a logbook can only be rebuilt from the
  board's activity history, which shows what was ticked off but not why or what
  the blockers were.

**Challenge and what I took from it:** The logbook is thin where we did not
write things down. We have dates for card updates but no stand-up or retrospective
notes, so the retrospective above had to be written from the board evidence. The
lesson is to record notes at the time.

**How it connects:** The logbook is where the user stories, backlogs and sprint
cards come together as dated work.

**What I would improve:** I would record each stand-up the same day, with a short
note on the card, so that the logbook shows who did what and when.

